      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on some walnut cabinet joinery and I'm having a bit of an issue. I'm getting some slight splintering at the tips of the pins when I'm cutting the dovetails. The grain is relatively straight, but it's still chipping. Any advice on chisel maintenance or how to better manage the grain to prevent this?",
